The fix is applied and all existing tests pass. Here's what changed:

**Bug:** `mergeImports` compared URLs with strict equality (`b.url === inc.url`), so `https://example.com/a` and `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` were treated as different URLs — causing the incoming bookmark to be added as a duplicate instead of merged.

**Fix in `src/import_merge.ts`:**
- Added `normalizeUrlForComparison(url)` helper that lowercases the hostname via the `URL` constructor (graceful fallback for invalid URLs).
- Changed the match lookup to compare normalized URLs: `normalizeUrlForComparison(b.url) === normalizeUrlForComparison(inc.url)`.

This ensures case-different hostnames are treated as the same URL, so the incoming bookmark is merged into the existing entry with unioned tags, not added as a duplicate.


